::PC_U05_L01_Q01::
Question ID: PC_U05_L01_Q01
MLA Standard: MLA.PC.VC.1
Question:
Which statement correctly describes complex-number work on the complex plane?
{
~A. Imaginary parts control horizontal position only.#This choice misses the two-part structure of complex numbers. Reconnect the real part to the horizontal coordinate and the imaginary part to the vertical coordinate.
=B. Real parts control horizontal position and imaginary parts control vertical position.#Correct. A complex number a + bi is represented by the point (a, b), so the real part is horizontal and the imaginary part is vertical.
~C. The complex plane does not use coordinates.#This choice misses the two-part structure of complex numbers. Reconnect the real part to the horizontal coordinate and the imaginary part to the vertical coordinate.
~D. The real part is ignored when graphing a complex number.#This choice misses the two-part structure of complex numbers. Reconnect the real part to the horizontal coordinate and the imaginary part to the vertical coordinate.
}
